# Commission 06H.4 — Historian Write Pipeline Recovery

## Objective

Diagnose and permanently resolve the failure of Ignition/Kymera to store historical tag values in the production InfluxDB bucket.

## Confirmed configuration

- Ignition: TP-IGN01, 172.16.81.201
- Ignition version: 8.3.4
- InfluxDB: 10.1.0.132:8086
- Organization: TBMC
- Bucket: TBMC-Sensor-Data
- Historian provider: InfluxDB
- Provider status: Enabled and RUNNING

## Confirmed diagnostic findings

The database-side diagnostic established:

- Remote connectivity and authenticated queries succeed.
- No records exist for HistorianTest_20261127_200012.
- None of the four expected values were stored: 10.25, 20.50, 30.75 and 40.00.
- Existing historical measurement: ignition-tp-ign01.default.
- Existing tag identifier: tagPath.
- Existing fields: bVal and quality.
- Historical records exist from November 4, 2026.
- SCADA TEMP trend reports Error_TimeoutExpired.

## 1. Diagnose the historical acquisition pipeline

Inspect and record:

- Installed Kymera module version and compatibility.
- Ignition and Kymera licensing/trial status.
- Effective historian provider configuration.
- Historian registration and execution status.
- Store and Forward engine status, pending records, quarantined records and write counters, where applicable.
- Gateway logs associated with Kymera, historian execution, authentication, sampling and historical queries.
- Effective configuration of the previous historian test tag from retained evidence.

Compare the current configuration against available November 4 deployment records.

Do not purge queued or quarantined historical data.

## 2. Isolate and correct the root cause

Determine whether historical samples are:

- Not being generated.
- Not being registered with the historian.
- Being buffered or quarantined.
- Being rejected by Kymera.
- Being rejected by InfluxDB.
- Being routed to an incorrect provider or destination.

Apply the minimum permanent correction necessary within the existing historian configuration.

Do not create another bucket, provider or database.

Do not upgrade modules or expand credential permissions without identifying and documenting the requirement first.

Preserve secure transport requirements and all existing production database records.

## 3. Verify historical acquisition

Create an isolated, uniquely named memory tag using the existing InfluxDB historian provider.

Verify effective history settings and registration.

Write four identifiable floating-point values at controlled intervals. Allow sufficient time for sampling, buffering and historian writes.

Capture:

- Tag value and quality.
- Historical registration.
- Sampling configuration.
- Store and Forward counters, if applicable.
- Historian write evidence.
- Actual historical query results.
- UTC timestamps.
- Expected InfluxDB measurement and tag path.

Retain the test tag until independent database verification is completed.

Do not substitute direct InfluxDB API writes for Ignition-originated historization.

## 4. Permanent production equipment test

After successful synthetic history verification, identify the existing Room 814 equipment:

BRX5-02-01 — TEMP

Trace its source OPC tag, existing KeyCPP reference and SCADA trend binding.

Verify actual source quality and instrument availability.

Permanently enable history on the appropriate existing tag required by the FAT-tested trend configuration. Avoid duplicate acquisition through both the process tag and KeyCPP reference.

Preserve the existing sampling and deadband design where documented.

Verify that historical values are stored and retrieved through the existing SCADA TEMP trend.

If physical measurement validity cannot be established, leave equipment history activation blocked and document the specific dependency.

## 5. Acceptance criteria

- Root cause identified and documented.
- Historical acquisition pipeline operational.
- Four Ignition-generated test samples independently verified in InfluxDB.
- Historical query through Ignition successful.
- Existing SCADA TEMP trend verified when valid equipment data is available.
- Successful configuration remains permanently enabled.
- Existing 36 OPC mappings preserved.
- Shared UDT definitions and FAT-tested graphics preserved.
- No unrelated production changes.

